# Peanut Butter Cupcakes

Based on [https://sallysbakingaddiction.com/peanut-butter-cupcakes](https://sallysbakingaddiction.com/peanut-butter-cupcakes)

{ rating="0" image="None" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

### Cupcakes

- [ ] 1.25 cups [all-purpose flour]{ ing="all-purpose-flour" }, spooned & leveled
- [ ] 1/2 tsp [baking soda]{ ing="baking-soda" }
- [ ] 1/4 tsp [salt]{ ing="salt" }
- [ ] 1/2 cup [canola or vegetable oil]{ ing="canola-or-vegetable-oil" }
- [ ] 1/2 cup [creamy peanut butter]{ ing="creamy-peanut-butter" }
- [ ] 1 cup packed [light or dark brown sugar]{ ing="brown-sugar" }
- [ ] 1 large [egg]{ ing="egg" }, at room temperature
- [ ] 1/3 cup [sour cream]{ ing="sour-cream" }, at room temperature
- [ ] 1.5 tsp [pure vanilla extract]{ ing="pure-vanilla-extract" }
- [ ] 3/4 cup [whole milk]{ ing="whole-milk" }, at room temperature
- [ ] 1/3 cup very finely crushed or chopped [peanuts]{ ing="peanuts" }

### Chocolate Peanut Butter Frosting

- [ ] 1 cup (16 Tbsps) [unsalted butter]{ ing="unsalted-butter" }, softened
- [ ] 3.5 cups [confectioners’ sugar]{ ing="confectioners-sugar" }
- [ ] 1/2 cup [unsweetened cocoa powder]{ ing="unsweetened-cocoa-powder" }
- [ ] 3 Tbsps [heavy cream]{ ing="heavy-cream" } or milk
- [ ] 1/3 cup [creamy peanut butter]{ ing="creamy-peanut-butter" }
- [ ] 1 tsp [pure vanilla extract]{ ing="pure-vanilla-extract" }
- [ ] 1/4 tsp [salt]{ ing="salt" }
- [ ] Optional: mini Reese’s [Peanut Butter Cups]{ ing="peanut-butter-cups" } or chopped peanuts for garnish

## Recipe

1. Preheat oven to 350°F (177°C). Line a 12-cup muffin pan with cupcake liners. Add 2-3 liners to a second pan since this recipe yields 14-15 cupcakes.
1. Whisk together [flour]{ ing="all-purpose-flour" }, [baking soda]{ ing="baking-soda" }, and [salt]{ ing="salt" } in a medium bowl; set aside.
1. Using a handheld or stand mixer, combine [oil]{ ing="canola-or-vegetable-oil" }, [peanut butter]{ ing="creamy-peanut-butter" }, [brown sugar]{ ing="brown-sugar" }, [egg]{ ing="egg" }, [sour cream]{ ing="sour-cream" }, and vanilla. Add dry ingredients, [milk]{ ing="whole-milk" }, and [peanuts]{ ing="peanuts" }; mix until combined without overmixing.
1. Fill liners two-thirds full. Bake 21-23 minutes until a toothpick inserted in the center comes out clean and tops spring back when touched. (Mini cupcakes: bake 11-13 minutes.) Cool completely before frosting.
1. Beat softened [butter]{ ing="unsalted-butter" } on medium speed until creamy, about 2 minutes.
1. Add [confectioners’ sugar]{ ing="confectioners-sugar" }, [cocoa powder]{ ing="unsweetened-cocoa-powder" }, and milk; beat on low for 30 seconds.
1. Add peanut butter, vanilla, and salt; beat on medium-high for 2 minutes until combined.
1. Adjust consistency with more confectioners’ sugar if too thin or [cream]{ ing="heavy-cream" }/milk if too thick.
1. Frost cooled cupcakes and garnish with [peanut butter cups]{ ing="peanut-butter-cups" } or chopped peanuts if desired.

## Notes

- Store leftovers covered in the refrigerator for up to 5 days
- A cupcake carrier is recommended for storing and transporting decorated cupcakes
